WEBVTT

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.520
I miss you...

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.770
...so much.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.330
Swimming the...

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.860
...seven seas.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:17.570
The water sparkles with 
the memories we had.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.550
A divine wind...

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.490
A divine wind has come!

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.580
You're the one who stopped the 
Mongol invasion of Japan?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.070
Ships sink when we sing.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.140
Are you the Lorelei or something?!

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.560
And why are you messing around 
with Japan's history?

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.300
I saved Japan in the end, so who cares?

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.800
Oh yeah, Muromi-san...

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.560
The Mongol invasion happened 
about eight hundred years ago.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.450
How old are—

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.560
I told you not to ask a 
lady stuff like that!

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.730
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.730
<b>Episode 2
"Muromi-san and the Legendary Sea Creatures"</b>

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.160
Takkun, do you have a cell phone?

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.120
I do...

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.710
Lemme see, lemme see.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:26.760
What are you gonna do with it?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.780
It's not like I have any 
interesting texts on it.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.330
Just lemme see.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.050
<b>You've received 1 new contact.</b>

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:35.750
Here you go.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:38.580
I gave you my number and email address.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.750
Now we can talk to each other anytime.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.930
Hold on a second!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.350
There are too many questions here...

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.780
Actually, I can't really 
think of what to ask.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.530
Everyone has a cell phone nowadays.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.310
I'm sure there are waterproof, 
shell-shaped cell phones out there.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.310
It's not like you should 
really be surprised here.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.110
I gave you my info, so text me?

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.340
I don't really text that much.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.320
I only use my phone when 
I have to, really.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.600
Just send me anything.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.560
To: Takkun
Sub: Sorry to say this out of the blue... 
I want to eat Muromi-san.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.770
Like what you had to eat, 
or what you're watching on TV.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.560
To: Muromi-san 
Huh? (Oh?)

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.570
To: Takkun 
Just kidding.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.570
To: Muromi-san
Oh, so you were kidding. (disappointed)

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:07.820
To: Takkun
Actually, I'm interested in that beautiful 
lone dandelion that blooms in the 
alley when I'm heading back home. 
The brief moment when I found what I was 
looking so hard for gives my day a fleeting 
moment of happiness. I'm sorry. Maybe
 I made you think something I shouldn't have.
 But I wouldn't just tell anyone about 
something like this.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.220
I wouldn't mind some sexts either.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.240
To: Muromi-san
Keep it to three lines.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.290
That's not happening!

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.920
If you want some special 
pictures of mine, you'll—

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.000
I don't need any!

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.700
I want to know what 
you're usually up to!

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.880
Fine.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.750
I'll do what I can.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.590
See you later!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.600
Why didn't you send me any texts?!

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:33.870
Uh...

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.610
I wasn't really sure what to send you.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.080
I sleep at night, and my phone's 
turned off when I'm at school.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.080
I sent you 372 texts that hit the 
5000 character limit.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.700
You sent too many, and 
they were all too long to read.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.700
Why didn't you send anything back?!

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.330
Takkun, you jerk!

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.420
Secret technique: Purple Sea Urchin Ball #1!

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.380
That was close!

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.340
Good bye urchin!

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.350
Forget you!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.590
She's going off in a butterfly of anger.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.170
Was there really a reason 
to get that mad?

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.140
I guess I'll just apologize 
next time I see her.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.330
That's Takkun?

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.810
He doesn't understand how 
a girl thinks at all.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.300
Right?

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.150
Hey, Muromi-san.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.170
What is it, Sumida-san?

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.530
You've been typing for a long time.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.570
Texting that human boy 
you were talking about?

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.040
Yeah.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.710
We ended up fighting and going our 
separate ways when we talked last.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.250
"So here's a quiz for you."

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.990
"Where do you think I am right now?"

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.600
"The correct answer is the Maldives."

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:39.890
"Have you heard of the Maldives before?"

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:41.130
"It's on the lower left side of India."

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:45.520
I want things to be normal 
next time I see him.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.240
"The ocean here is beautiful."

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.810
"I guess you'd call it cider blue."

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.840
"The sunset's really romantic, too."

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.020
"I'd like to watch it with you sometime."

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.150
"I'll be back tomorrow."

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:56.600
"I'll bring you back something."

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.820
Guys really go for it if you 
use hearts in your texts.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.590
You're pretty into this guy, 
even though he's a kid.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.110
Time for a service shot.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.160
And send.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.070
So, things looking good with him?

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.450
I'm not sure...

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.600
He's still a boy, you know?

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.170
Oh, he responded!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.250
What'd he say?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.550
"Okay."

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.820
<i>That's not going anywhere.</i>

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.810
Looks like my first big one in a while!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.490
It's Muromi-san again?!

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.680
Ouch.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.410
You're Takkun, right?

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.560
Muromi isn't here yet?

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.350
I can't get this out.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:00.670
There's a hook on this.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.380
I thought you might 
be with Muromi-san.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.340
I'm surprised that I'm not 
very surprised anymore.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.470
I guess I'll ask...

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.150
Who are you?!

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:12.140
Me?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.350
I'm Levia.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.600
I'm meeting up with Muromi here today.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.420
Meeting up with her?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.190
She told me to meet at the fishing boy.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.320
<i>She's treating me like that 
dog statue in Shibuya</i>

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.820
<i>that people use as a meeting spot.</i>

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.110
It looks like you guys have 
already introduced yourselves.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.870
Oh, Muromi! It's been a while!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.250
It's been a while!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:33.640
<b>Been a while!</b>

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.440
How do you two know each other?

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:37.710
Are you sisters?

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.620
Levia-san's my elder from back home.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.370
She's helped me out a lot.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.290
Back home?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.340
Where are you from, Levia-san?

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.510
Kokura.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.260
Oh, that's why you say 
stuff like Lum-chan.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.220
<b>Kokura</b>

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.220
This is Kokura!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.860
Wait... Levia-san...

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:53.850
San...

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:55.090
Huh?!

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.220
The Leviathan!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.620
Why did you start screaming 
out of nowhere?

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.520
You didn't really have to go 
out of your way to say that.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:03.000
The Leviathan.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.330
A giant sea monster referenced 
in the Christian Old Testament.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.810
It has tough scales and sharp teeth, 
and breathes fire from its mouth.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.910
The real thing doesn't quite 
match the description.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.940
No, when she goes into combat mode,

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.890
she gets bigger and breathes lots of fire.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:20.040
I haven't transformed for 
the past few hundred years.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.250
I should have a picture of Levia-san 
in action on my cell here.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.170
Hold on a second.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.560
Oh, don't. It's embarrassing.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.670
How many centuries have you had 
phones with cameras, anyway?

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:30.050
Here it is.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.590
This is Levia-san.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.510
Pretty cool, huh?

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.050
What's going on in this picture?!

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.700
Levia-san, do you remember?

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.890
Oh, I remember that.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.440
That sure brings back memories.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.800
That was from back when we 
destroyed the Mu continent.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.720
When the people from Mu

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.140
used their super-advanced science to 
attempt to overthrow the gods,

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.320
I was the head of the attack party.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:57.990
Yeah, we were helping out the Olympus 
deities and the Valhalla Federation.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.960
Didn't Odin and Zeus sink the 
continent by working together?

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.150
That really brings back memories.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.240
I remember that.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.580
They're talking about 
divine retribution...

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.590
Anyway, that's enough reminiscing.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.770
Levia-san, where do you want to go?

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.810
I want to head to Kagoshima.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.080
I want to have some of 
that Shirokuma dessert.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.040
Shirokuma is shaved ice, you know?

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.600
Takkun, you wanna come?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.150
I'm good.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.390
The Satsuma area there 
is known for its pigs.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.150
The sweet potato wine is excellent.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.490
That sounds good.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.030
I can't wait.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.270
There were a lot of myths in there...

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:39.670
Muromi-san!

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:44.250
Who was playing with fireworks and 
didn't clean up after themselves?

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.160
You know you're refined when 
you're playing with fireworks

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.420
when it's still light out.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.470
It was you guys!

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.850
Oh, Takkun. You should join us.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.870
That was dangerous! God...

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.310
You shouldn't point a lighted 
rocket-style firework at someone.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.560
Gosh, you're such a downer.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.880
Pick up all the trash you've 
left and put it in here!

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:10.530
Hurry up!

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.440
R-Right!

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.740
What's wrong?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.610
You don't normally use 
that tone of voice.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:20.180
Of course I'll get mad if you foul up

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.600
the place where I spend my free time.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.850
Why would you mess up the ocean when you're

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.960
the ones who'll be hurting most if it's dirty?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:30.080
Well, we started talking about doing 
 fireworks, and got all excited...

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.170
After kind of reminiscing, I wanted 
to give it a shot, too, so...

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.420
<i>Onee-tan, they're pretty!</i>

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.760
<i>Yay, fireworks!</i>

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.980
<i>Tamaya!</i>

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.000
<i>It's nice to watch some 
fireworks while drinking beer.</i>

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.020
<i>Pretty refined.</i>

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.990
Wait, those aren't fireworks, 
that's the Battle of Troy!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.570
And with the "Tamaya" shouting 
and the canned beer...

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.600
We picked up all the trash.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.440
Oh, good work.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.790
So you two aren't scared of fire?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.840
Animals are usually afraid of it.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.050
I guess Levia-san would 
be an exception there.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.070
What about you, Muromi-san?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.870
I like fireworks because they're pretty.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:18.220
But I don't really have a lot 
of good memories with fire.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.370
Oh, are you talking about that time?

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:21.180
What?

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.560
I got forced into a witch trial 
because my bottom half is fish.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.680
In France in the middle ages.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.410
Fire doesn't really affect me,

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.250
but there were some pretty 
traumatic things that happened.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.570
The humans there were 
scarier than the fire!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:39.410
Well, as punishment, I rained 
fire down on everyone involved.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.480
I think that's why the witch 
trials were abolished, right?

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.970
You're the scariest one of them all.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.900
Anyway, I think I'm going to get going.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.940
I had plenty of fun here in Japan.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.090
Where are you going?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:57.240
I was thinking of relaxing in Northern 
Europe while watching aurora borealis.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.260
You lead a life so slow, it makes me jealous.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.440
Muromi, stay well.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.970
If you need me for anything, 
call me anytime.

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.260
People don't see each other 
off like that in Japan...

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:09.730
Takkun, you too!

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.640
Huh? Me, too?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.570
She might run around all cheerful-like, 
but she's pretty lonely at heart.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.150
Give her as much attention as you can.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.420
Levia-san has a lot more sides 
to her than I thought.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.950
I can't tell if she's laid 
back or has it together.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.350
She's been alive for a 
long time, you know?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.920
So Takkun...

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.890
It's a lot more fun doing 
fireworks at night.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:47.950
Yeah.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:51.790
Let's go to a hot spring.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:52.410
Sure.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.520
How about the Minakami and 
Kusatsu hot springs?

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.110
I want to go to a bigger hot spring.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:55.920
Where?

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.110
The ocean itself!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.480
I'll heat up all these waters for us!

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.190
Hellfire, go!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:05.990
Next time: 
"Muromi-san and Old Memories"

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.660
Levia-san, don't do it!

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.310
And then the Earth went up in flames.
